id: pmc-stable-itemless-check
title: Keep changelog checks stable when an empty release is tagged
description: Full-history checks add an empty Unreleased section after a package release tag appears.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-changelog#333"
created_at: "2026-11-07T22:05:29.088Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T05:50:09.467Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Empty and item-bearing releases render byte-identically across tag publication; empty Unreleased does not displace releases; Randomized tests and revert proof cover aliases, older commits, same-day versions and no-git trackers; Document include-empty; audit git-optional dependency notes and record follow-up when unsupported; Public pm-jira, pm-ops and third tracker evidence; targeted tests, typecheck and npm/Bun CI release gates"
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T22:05:31.520Z",pi-agent,"Closed pmc-itemless-pending covers git-derived notes, not include-empty visibility. Public pm-jira main 9ff81121748701c3f95e40e758ec28d89ac73805 reproduces the empty Unreleased diff. Current generator also differs from that consumer historical baseline in dependency notes and old item ordering; measure those separately from tag-only stability."
  "2026-11-07T22:07:05.913Z",pi-agent,"Selection fix omits empty Unreleased before limits on all item visibility paths, retaining empty versioned releases. Tag audit found default v-only discovery and duplicate calendar aliases; normalize equivalent tags into one window and accept unprefixed version tags by default. Different historical versions or changed commit boundaries are real release-history changes, so arbitrary tag-set independence is impossible; README documents that boundary and immutable milestone alternative. Git-optional merged-change receipt design is tracked in pmc-portable-change-receipts; no new git-only notes logic."
  "2026-11-07T22:14:21.318Z",pi-agent,"Targeted generator/itemless/release-context/stability suite: 212 tests passed, zero failures/skips. Typecheck, test compilation and docstring lint passed (265 declarations). Disposable behavioral reverts: restoring empty Unreleased visibility fails both property and slot-selection regressions (2 failures); restoring v-only discovery fails property (1); restoring duplicate alias windows fails property (1). Each fixed/restored run passes both selected tests. Pinned pm test --run --progress --only-last ran the proof successfully; test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains counts without package-owned run artefacts. pm-ops uses scripts/pm-changelog.ts to strip empty Unreleased; its passing checks do not show an item-bearing exemption."
  "2026-11-07T22:16:30.146Z",pi-agent,"Real public data: pm-jira main/release 9ff8112, pm-ops release 274c158 (source main 091124b), and pm-ado release 0b3d5a3 (source main 56c40e9) all produce identical bytes before/after their tags. Generated baseline checks pass 0/0 for all three. Original release files: pm-ado passes 0/0; pm-jira remains 1/1 from historical notes/order migration, pm-ops direct generator remains 1/1 from notes plus repository wrapper wording. Do not claim unchanged-file acceptance for those two; pmc-consumer-projection-migration records it. Final focused CLI/help/property suite passed 41/41, zero skips. Exact source heads, bytes, digests and reproduction command are in docs/stable-check-evidence.md. The task-specific tag flip is fixed, with consumer migration explicitly outstanding."
  "2026-11-07T22:18:07.554Z",pi-agent,"Final cleanup removes the empty-grouping placeholder entirely so no unused versioned fallback survives the new empty-Unreleased contract. Updated the prior coverage regression to assert title-only output. Final property plus generator branch suite: 72 passed, zero failed/skipped; typecheck, test compilation, docstring lint (42 files, 265 declarations), and whitespace checks pass. Full release evidence is delegated to unchanged CI npm and Bun release:check gates on Node 22/26. Consumer migration and portable receipt designs remain open follow-ups. Claim released for orchestrator review; no item was closed."
  "2026-11-07T22:25:50.033Z",pi-agent,"Review found a valid dependency-aware visibility edge: with explicit dependency notes and limit 1, Unreleased can contain notes while item diagnostics dropped it and reported older items. Rendering, visibleChangelogItems and explain now reuse dependency-aware section construction before candidate filtering and limits. Add a real-git regression for both include-empty settings and extend disposable revert proofs for the diagnostic/item-list paths. No new Git-only notes source is introduced."
  "2026-11-07T22:31:22.226Z",pi-agent,"PR #333 review correction verified: final targeted command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/stable-itemless-check.test.ts test/generator.test.ts test/generator-coverage.test.ts test/itemless-pending.test.ts test/release-context.test.ts passes 281/281, zero failures/skips. Typecheck and test compilation pass; docstring lint covers 266 declarations. Pinned pm test --run --progress --only-last passes all five disposable behavioral reverts in 126.706 seconds: failure counts 2/1/1/1/1, with every fixed/restored test passing. The extra reverts independently remove dependency-aware explanation and item-list selection. Initial CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/42420049972 was queued before starting on the superseded head; full npm/Bun gate evidence must come from the corrected PR head. Current main consumer migration limits remain documented and unchanged."
  "2026-11-07T22:42:24.282Z",pi-agent,"Final tag audit found equal commit timestamps in same-day releases: lexical tag ordering can put the base version ahead of its -2 successor after publication. Extend the randomized property with equal-boundary releases and choose tag spellings independently of the suffix cases. Add direct comparator assertions and a same-instant counter ordering guard, retaining ordinary/invalid timestamp name ordering. Extend the behavioral proof to remove that guard independently."
  "2026-11-07T22:48:16.233Z",pi-agent,"Equal-time release audit completed: enhanced property plus direct comparator test fail 2/44 before the guard and pass 44/44 after it. Final combined five-file targeted suite passes 282/282, zero failures/skips, in 160.722 seconds. Typecheck/test compilation/docstring lint pass (266 declarations). Six disposable behavioral reverts pass via pinned pm test in 200.507 seconds, with expected failure counts 2/1/1/1/1/1 and every fixed/restored run green. Public pm-jira/pm-ops/pm-ado tag metadata has zero affected same-day/equal-time pairs, so the measured snapshot bytes remain unchanged. The CI run for prior head 006b0ca remains in lifecycle validation at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/42421046425; npm and Bun full release gates have not run yet. Corrected-head gates remain required; do not treat earlier CodeQL or local targeted tests as full-gate approval."
  "2026-11-07T22:50:02.185Z",pi-agent,"CI cutoff receipt after the allowed 30-minute window: code head 5cf94f2db8fa68eecbb0a5e38d8e61a7e32daa41 has CI lifecycle in progress at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/42422378771 and CodeQL in progress at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/42422378874. The Node 22/26 npm and Bun release:check matrix has not completed: 0/4 full gates verified, no full-suite pass counts or coverage claimed. Local source validation is 282/282 and six successful behavioral revert proofs. This append-only receipt requires a fresh exact-head CI run; the PR checks and final report identify that run. No further CI waiting after this receipt. Orchestrator must verify final-head gates and consumer migration limits before closing the item or merging."
  "2026-11-07T23:42:03.747Z",codex-sol,"Continuation review round: reuse PR #333 and this item; branch is current with origin/main (zero commits behind), clean, and matches its remote. Confirmed three findings: release ordering must be total and alias-invariant; filesystem fixtures must not require case-only refs; every include-empty option description must match rendering. Audit the whole package and add adversarial properties plus disposable revert proofs before unchanged npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-11-07T23:48:54.746Z",codex-sol,"Review class audit: release-context listReleaseTags is the shared tag sort for SDK, standalone CLI and both extension commands; all rendering/JSON/summary/visibility paths consume its windows. Other package sorts use tracker keys or version segments, not the pair-dependent tag counter/name fallback. Found one case-only loose-ref fixture creation and routed all alias additions through a case-insensitive fixture helper; uppercase-only refs remain exercised. Audited README, usage docs, SDK types, CLI help and both extension flag declarations; corrected the stale options-table row and clarified historical-window prose. New property covers 56 adversarial names, every triple at valid/invalid timestamps, 128 permutations and alias additions. Focused three-file suite passes 53/53 with zero skips; typecheck, test compilation and docstring lint pass. Disposable review reverts independently restore old pair ordering, case-sensitive ref matching and stale docs: each yields 1 assertion failure; every fixed/restored test passes. The pinned pm linked runner also passed the three proofs (15.307 seconds); test-result tracking is disabled, so no run artifacts enter the package tracker."
  "2026-11-07T23:50:39.075Z",codex-sol,"Packed review acceptance passes via node scripts/accept-stable-review.ts: the same SHA-512 artifact is installed with npm and Bun, each preserving seven projections after publishing the adversarial numeric/prerelease alias. Checks include Node/Bun SDKs, standalone Markdown/JSON, installed extension Markdown/JSON/TOON summary with diagnostics, and unchanged-file checks on both runtimes. Archive SHA-512: 076f0a19ce85098c3184415d0722e9a7709b86739b37ba39fb8f5e49fcfa113ebddb734598ea24e38ee6272baa29ade5739df397cdd1a69aee8d12ade5900373. The existing non-git tracker regression also passes with no Git executable. Full npm then Bun release gates run sequentially with fresh HOME, disabled global/system Git config and a credential-free child environment; coverage runner uses two workers."
  "2026-11-07T23:57:27.063Z",codex-sol,"Prior-head CI finished after the earlier cutoff: run 42422488295 passed lifecycle but both Node 22/26 npm gates failed two old fixtures (claim-audit empty unversioned claim; extension parity expecting empty Unreleased from the package tracker). Stopped the first local full run when these concrete failures were discovered; it is canceled evidence, not a pass. Preserve all existing assertions: give the empty claim an explicit version, add a zero-claim assertion for empty Unreleased, and move pending-release parity into a real scratch tracker/Git history with delivered pending work. This removes reliance on mutable package history without weakening the parity or release-heading checks. Focus these cases before restarting the unchanged full gates."
  "2026-11-08T00:41:49.333Z",codex-sol,"Full npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME/Git config and two workers: 1022 tests, 0 failures, 0 skips; all 28 configured source files reported at 100% lines/branches/functions. Production audit found 0 vulnerabilities; pack allowlist/content scan, changelog/link check, release-date and publication-attestation checks passed. The two prior-head CI fixture failures are fixed and pass within this full run. Bun run release:check is now running sequentially on the same source. Statement coverage is not independently measured by this gate."
  "2026-11-08T01:07:42.191Z",codex-sol,"Final review validation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass on unchanged source, sequentially with two workers and isolated HOME/Git config. Each reports 1022 passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped; all 28 required sources at 100% lines/branches/functions. Each production audit has 0 vulnerabilities; both package allowlist/content scans cover 107 files with 0 failures; changelog/link, release-date and publication-attestation checks pass. Focused review tests pass 53/53; the two retained CI fixture assertions pass 2/2 and in both full gates. Three disposable review reverts fail independently (1 each), with all fixed/restored cases passing through the pinned pm runner. Packed npm/Bun consumers preserve seven projections each and Node/Bun check mode. No test or threshold was removed or reduced. Origin/main is still current (zero commits behind). Existing consumer migration and portable-receipt follow-ups are retained without duplicates. Release this implementation claim for orchestrator verification; keep the item in progress. Fresh pushed-head CI and re-review remain required before closure or merge."
  "2026-11-08T11:26:08.063Z",codex-sol,"Continuation preserves all five existing commits and PR #333. Current remote head 63b4d4e passed CI lifecycle and both Node 22/26 matrix jobs. Two remaining review findings are valid: build current source before packing with lifecycle scripts disabled; isolate Git fixture commands from inherited repository-location overrides. Add focused regressions and isolated revert proofs, rerun packed npm/Bun acceptance, then finish tracker writes before fresh exact-head CI. Existing consumer projection migration and git-optional receipt designs remain separate follow-ups."
  "2026-11-08T11:32:39.359Z",codex-sol,"Final continuation results: focused release-context/stability/docs/fixture suite passes 54/54, zero failures/skips; the complete fixture file retains both existing regressions and passes 3/3, also through pinned pm test --run --progress. Typecheck, test compilation, docstring lint (45 files, 266 declarations) and whitespace checks pass. Pinned pm test --run --progress --match prove-stable-fixture-hygiene passes in 125.288 seconds: four independent old behaviors fail (inherited Git locations, alias discovery override, alias creation override, skipped build with poisoned emitted CLI), with every fixed/restored run passing. Restored real npm/Bun consumers each preserve seven projections and Node/Bun check mode on one packed artifact; SHA-512 c41a0032d5d5341314dfec4734789c27a3c2e337dbd7fc30c25706ef643b57ffc2782df572ff38adbe7862f2212f7640654e72ee9e7954f7ea946b939bc849be. Fresh public clones reproduce all three prior release snapshot byte hashes: generated checks pass before/after each tag; original committed files remain fail/fail for pm-jira and direct pm-ops, pass/pass for pm-ado. Current public main heads and exact snapshots are documented in docs/stable-check-evidence.md. Earlier head 63b4d4e passed CI 42432962949 lifecycle and all four npm/Bun release gates on Node 22/26; its local full gates recorded 1022/1022, not a count for this added regression. Fresh CI at the final pushed head remains required. The two review threads are left open for the orchestrator; no replies or resolutions were sent. Existing follow-ups remain unchanged and no items are closed."
  "2026-11-08T12:03:15.174Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator, CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc61AeV3 (docs/stable-check-evidence.md:78): the evidence report now says that final-head npm and Bun release gates must provide the full-suite evidence before merge, and that the completed matrix recorded there ran on a prior head. Documentation only; no behaviour change."
  "2026-11-09T05:50:09.467Z","harness:claude-code","Orchestrator fix for CodeRabbit threads PRRT_kwDOSfkApc61A4h_ and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc61A4iB: test/git-fixture.ts exports fixtureEnvironment(), and the fixture git tag (extension parity test), git commit and git tag --list (alias fixture test) now run with it. Revert proof: with an exported hostile GIT_DIR (empty bare repo) the alias fixture test fails reverted (commit lands in the outer repository) and passes fixed. The parity test still needs a real work tree under a hostile GIT_DIR because the production CLI subprocess reads GIT_DIR on purpose."
